{
  "subject": "fix: hand focus back when overlays close",
  "capturedAt": "2026-09-21T11:44:43.336Z",
  "defect": "Overlays (bottom sheet, command palette, select, morph select, the attachment image preview and the swap token picker) took focus, or let it fall away, and never handed it back when they closed. WebKit does not focus a button on click, so in Safari focus ended on <body> after a mouse-opened overlay closed; in Chrome the overlays that moved focus into themselves stranded it on <body> on both paths.",
  "method": "Per overlay, per browser, per build, two paths. Mouse: click the trigger with no prior focus call, wait for the overlay, press Escape, wait, read document.activeElement. Keyboard: focus the trigger through window.__audit.focusAt(), press Enter, wait, press Escape, wait, read document.activeElement. Every path starts from a fresh page load; the preview is scrolled so its top sits 96 px below the viewport top.",
  "environment": {
    "machine": "macOS 26.6.2",
    "chrome": {
      "version": "153.0.8010.50",
      "driver": "Playwright, chromium.launch({ channel: \"chrome\", headless: false })",
      "viewport": "1440x900"
    },
    "safari": {
      "version": "26.6.2",
      "driver": "safaridriver (W3C WebDriver) on port 4491",
      "viewport": "1440x900"
    }
  },
  "builds": {
    "before": {
      "label": "upstream main",
      "origin": "http://localhost:3300",
      "servedFrom": "wt/upstream-main"
    },
    "after": {
      "label": "PR branch fix/focus-return-on-close",
      "origin": "http://localhost:3301",
      "servedFrom": "wt/focus-return-on-close"
    }
  },
  "knownLimitation": "The bottom-sheet and command-palette demos open from plain consumer-owned onClick triggers that the library never sees, so there is nothing for the component to capture when WebKit leaves the click unfocused. On the mouse path in Safari both still end on <body> after the fix; their keyboard path returns to the trigger.",
